        "original_id": "20d17396-a8c8-5e58-8a3b-ccb406d1fa03",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Lucrezia Borgia, Il pirata, Bertram, ou le Pirate, Raimonde\n- People: Gaetano Donizetti, Vincenzo Bellini, Felice Romani, Charles Nodier, Isidore Justin Séverin Taylor\n- Topics: Opera, libretto, mélodrame\n\nFacts:\n- In 1826, Charles Nodier and Isidore Justin Séverin Taylor created the three-act mélodrame Bertram, ou le Pirate and Raimonde, which later served as source material for Il pirata.\n- Lucrezia Borgia is a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts by Gaetano Donizetti.\n- Il pirata is an opera in two acts by Vincenzo Bellini.\n- Il pirata has an Italian libretto by Felice Romani.\n- Il pirata was based on the 1826 three-act mélodrame Bertram, ou le Pirate by Charles Nodier and Raimonde by Isidore Justin Séverin Taylor.",
